  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness — specifically, whether a lottery has a greater portion of probability on favorable outcomes (i.e., left-skewed). In this problem, both lotteries are right-skewed (more probability on 0), so no lottery is left-skewed. Therefore, the reason cannot be applied. The individual's verbal report focuses on the likelihood of winning (i.e., the probability of a positive outcome), not on skewness. There is no mention of distribution shape, favorable vs unfavorable outcomes, or any reasoning about left-skewness. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reason is not triggered by the problem structure, and the reported justification is unrelated to skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
